# How Rabbit Brought Fire

In the beginning the people had no fire, and the *Weasels* kept it for themselves.

> I can run and swim faster than the Weasels, and I am also a *good dancer*. — Rabbit, to the council

```
Seed the chance with 42.
```

So he danced close to the fire until the pine tar in his hair caught, and ran home (the hollow tree) with his head ablaze.

